WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.391 --> 00:00:19.313
was just getting my things packed up when Holmes returned from his excursions.

2
00:00:20.173 --> 00:00:24.494
I noticed that he was carrying a sheet of blue paper in his hand, but before I could

3
00:00:24.574 --> 00:00:29.095
ask him how his investigation had progressed, Holmes made an announcement.

4
00:00:29.115 --> 00:00:34.890
"Watson," he said, "I have uncovered a very interesting set of facts.

5
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:42.094
First, I spoke with a physician at the hospital library about the mysterious death of Miss Julia Stoner.

6
00:00:43.015 --> 00:00:47.918
Then, I paid a visit to city hall, where I reviewed the will of the deceased wife."

7
00:00:48.598 --> 00:00:49.599
"Our client's mother?"

8
00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:50.799
I inquired.

9
00:00:50.819 --> 00:00:54.422
"Yes, it seems that she left Dr.

10
00:00:54.502 --> 00:01:02.041
Roylott an income of almost 1,100 pounds; however, the sum has shrunk slightly over the years due to

11
00:01:02.101 --> 00:01:08.983
inflation. Each daughter can claim an income of 250 pounds upon her marriage, which would leave the widower

12
00:01:09.043 --> 00:01:10.003
with very little.

13
00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:16.445
Since he no longer practices medicine and is responsible for the care of the family estate, it is

14
00:01:16.525 --> 00:01:20.246
clear that he would end up in poverty in the event that his stepdaughters wed."

15
00:01:20.986 --> 00:01:24.427
"This is definitely a motive for the crime, Holmes," I stated.

16
00:01:25.207 --> 00:01:30.517
My friend and associate nodded in agreement and quickly gathered his things to prepare for our trip to

17
00:01:30.577 --> 00:01:31.277
Stoke Moran.

18
00:01:32.137 --> 00:01:37.099
Then we left the house on Baker Street by cab and caught the afternoon train from Waterloo to

19
00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:40.379
Leatherhead, a small town several miles from the mansion.

20
00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.980
At Leatherhead we hired a carriage to take us to the property.

21
00:01:44.721 --> 00:01:49.562
Holmes spent the entire trip sitting with his arms folded in front of his chest and his hat

22
00:01:49.602 --> 00:01:50.862
pulled down over his eyes.

23
00:01:51.763 --> 00:01:56.724
After several miles the driver shouted out, "It's over there, sirs, just beyond the village."

24
00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.262
Holmes immediately sat upright and adjusted his hat.

25
00:02:01.063 --> 00:02:05.607
About a mile to the east was a rolling hill covered in a thick grove of trees through

26
00:02:05.647 --> 00:02:07.849
which the peak of a gray rooftop was visible.

27
00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:09.371
"Stoke Moran?"

28
00:02:09.911 --> 00:02:10.512
Holmes asked.

29
00:02:10.532 --> 00:02:12.554
"Yes, the home of Dr.

30
00:02:12.594 --> 00:02:13.715
Grimesby Roylott, sir.

31
00:02:14.335 --> 00:02:16.657
I could take you around to the front door if you'd like.

32
00:02:17.238 --> 00:02:20.581
But it's faster if I drop you here and you walk in along the footpath.

33
00:02:21.161 --> 00:02:23.844
I believe that's Miss Stoner walking there right now."

34
00:02:24.588 --> 00:02:27.971
Holmes paid the fare, and the two of us climbed out of the carriage.

35
00:02:28.691 --> 00:02:30.233
Miss Stoner hurried over to greet us.

36
00:02:30.253 --> 00:02:33.836
"I have been eagerly awaiting your arrival," she said.

37
00:02:33.856 --> 00:02:36.758
"Dr. Roylott should be gone for the rest of the day."

38
00:02:36.778 --> 00:02:39.380
"Yes," replied Holmes.

39
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.623
"We have had the pleasure of making the doctor's acquaintance."

40
00:02:43.844 --> 00:02:44.724
"Oh, good heavens!"

41
00:02:45.385 --> 00:02:47.446
Miss Stoner exclaimed with great surprise.

42
00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.408
"Has he followed me then?

43
00:02:50.049 --> 00:02:51.750
I never know when I am safe from him.

44
00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.972
What will I say when he returns?"

45
00:02:54.728 --> 00:02:58.790
"Your safety is our greatest concern," Holmes said consolingly.

46
00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:01.511
"You must keep your door locked tonight.

47
00:03:02.011 --> 00:03:04.633
If he becomes violent, is there somewhere you can go?"

48
00:03:04.653 --> 00:03:08.254
"I have an aunt in the village," said Miss Stoner.

49
00:03:08.274 --> 00:03:12.636
"If need be," said Holmes, "we'll take you there."

50
00:03:13.417 --> 00:03:19.019
Miss Stoner seemed quite relieved by this, but she continued to talk about her fears as we walked

51
00:03:19.079 --> 00:03:20.600
across the field toward the house.

52
00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.422
As we neared the property, I noticed that it was quite old and run-down.

53
00:03:26.163 --> 00:03:28.924
Some of the windows and doors were covered with wooden boards.

54
00:03:29.625 --> 00:03:34.187
The mansion's gray bricks were covered in thick moss, and part of the roof had caved in.

55
00:03:35.208 --> 00:03:40.190
The central portion, however, was more modern, and a curl of blue smoke escaped from the chimney.

56
00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:43.912
"There are shutters on the windows," Holmes observed.

57
00:03:43.932 --> 00:03:50.396
"Yes, I bar them shut every night before bed to keep the animals out," explained Miss Stoner.

58
00:03:51.168 --> 00:03:53.970
Holmes strolled over to the windows and examined them carefully.

59
00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:58.874
"There doesn't seem to be any way to break in from the outside," he said.

60
00:03:58.894 --> 00:04:02.817
"That would likely rule out any involvement by the Gypsies.

61
00:04:03.538 --> 00:04:07.441
Now, did you say that your stepfather was doing some renovations?"

62
00:04:08.242 --> 00:04:10.944
"Yes, but no work has been done so far.

63
00:04:11.624 --> 00:04:14.467
I fear it's just an excuse to get me to change rooms."

64
00:04:15.247 --> 00:04:20.091
Holmes continued to examine the physical structure of the house as we walked through the front door and

65
00:04:20.131 --> 00:04:20.832
down the hallway.

66
00:04:21.724 --> 00:04:24.206
I noticed three doors along the left-hand side.

67
00:04:24.226 --> 00:04:26.247
"Where is your room?"

68
00:04:26.828 --> 00:04:28.009
Holmes asked our client.

69
00:04:28.029 --> 00:04:31.551
"My room is at the end of the hall," she responded.

70
00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:32.792
"Follow me."

71
00:04:33.553 --> 00:04:37.295
Miss Stoner's room was cold and rather shabby, but otherwise ordinary.

72
00:04:37.836 --> 00:04:40.898
There was nothing to note, so we quickly moved into the middle room.

73
00:04:41.518 --> 00:04:44.160
"This one belonged to Julia," she explained.

74
00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.422
"But I have moved my things in here now."

75
00:04:46.442 --> 00:04:49.324
"This is odd," said Holmes.

76
00:04:49.952 --> 00:04:53.854
He took his magnifying glass out of his coat pocket and began to examine the floor.

77
00:04:53.874 --> 00:04:59.577
"The bed is bolted to the floor, preventing it from being moved to another location.

78
00:05:00.258 --> 00:05:04.700
Hmm here is also a bell rope hanging down from the ceiling to the bed.

79
00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.421
Didn't you say you had no servants?"

80
00:05:08.182 --> 00:05:09.282
"Yes, that is correct.

81
00:05:09.763 --> 00:05:11.804
We haven't had a servant in several months."

82
00:05:12.824 --> 00:05:16.486
Holmes pulled the cord and announced, "Why, it's a fake!

83
00:05:16.906 --> 00:05:17.987
It doesn't ring at all.

84
00:05:19.916 --> 00:05:22.238
Interesting Look up here, Watson, near the ceiling.

85
00:05:22.878 --> 00:05:27.481
There is a small square window through the wall connecting this room to the one next to it.

86
00:05:28.342 --> 00:05:34.086
I would guess that it could be part of the ventilation system—you see, there is a metal door

87
00:05:34.126 --> 00:05:38.789
that can be closed to keep out the cold air—but it doesn't seem to be connected to the

88
00:05:38.849 --> 00:05:41.971
outside. I wonder what it could be for?"

89
00:05:41.991 --> 00:05:46.414
"I don't know," Miss Stoner said, sounding increasingly worried.

90
00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:48.776
"It was put in about three years ago.

91
00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:50.741
The room next door is Dr.

92
00:05:50.782 --> 00:05:55.366
Roylott's." At this announcement Holmes raised his eyebrows and nodded his head.

93
00:05:56.246 --> 00:06:01.892
I was sure that he had deduced something important from the evidence—something that I could not figure out

94
00:06:01.952 --> 00:06:02.472
on my own.

95
00:06:03.173 --> 00:06:06.095
Holmes could often see answers where others could not.

96
00:06:07.156 --> 00:06:10.499
When Holmes was finished examining Julia's room, we moved into Dr.

97
00:06:10.559 --> 00:06:12.901
Roylott's room to complete our investigation.

98
00:06:13.862 --> 00:06:19.287
There we discovered a filing cabinet, a single bed, and other regular items that one would expect to

99
00:06:19.347 --> 00:06:20.188
find in a bedroom.

100
00:06:21.029 --> 00:06:25.833
Holmes, however, spent a long time examining an old wooden chair that sat beside the bed.

101
00:06:26.513 --> 00:06:29.195
He also made several unusual observations.

102
00:06:29.215 --> 00:06:33.099
"There is a saucer of milk on the floor," he noted.

103
00:06:33.119 --> 00:06:35.261
"Miss Stoner, do you have a cat?"

104
00:06:35.961 --> 00:06:37.923
"No, we do not," she replied.

105
00:06:37.943 --> 00:06:39.644
"Could it be for the cheetah?"

106
00:06:40.305 --> 00:06:40.705
I asked.

107
00:06:40.725 --> 00:06:43.788
"I don't think so," said Holmes.

108
00:06:44.372 --> 00:06:47.233
"It would be too small to satisfy a beast that big.

109
00:06:47.753 --> 00:06:50.994
Look here," he said, pointing to the head of the bed.

110
00:06:51.774 --> 00:06:56.636
Hanging from the bedpost was what looked like a dog's leash that had been curled up at the

111
00:06:56.736 --> 00:06:57.536
end into a loop.

112
00:06:57.556 --> 00:07:00.117
"I'm getting quite concerned.

113
00:07:00.817 --> 00:07:04.338
I fear any man who uses his intelligence for evil deeds."

114
00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:07.639
Holmes' comment sent a shiver up my spine.

115
00:07:08.379 --> 00:07:11.960
For the first time, I began to realize how much danger we were actually in.

116
00:07:12.748 --> 00:07:15.870
Thank goodness I had remembered to put my pistol in my bag.

117
00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:23.534
"Miss Stoner," Holmes said in a soft, reassuring voice, "tonight you must prepare for bed as usual.

118
00:07:24.294 --> 00:07:25.215
But do not sleep.

119
00:07:25.715 --> 00:07:28.857
Instead I want you to wait until you hear Dr.

120
00:07:28.937 --> 00:07:30.198
Roylott prepare for bed.

121
00:07:31.038 --> 00:07:36.061
When you think he is asleep, I want you to place your lantern in Julia's open window and

122
00:07:36.101 --> 00:07:38.102
escape to your own room down the hall.

123
00:07:38.842 --> 00:07:41.484
Don't forget to lock your doors and bar your shutters.

124
00:07:41.972 --> 00:07:43.613
We will be watching from the village.

125
00:07:44.253 --> 00:07:48.476
When we see your lantern, we will sneak through Julia's window and spend the night in the room.

126
00:07:49.256 --> 00:07:50.517
Now let's go, Watson.

127
00:07:51.217 --> 00:07:53.599
We will take a room at the inn and wait for the signal.

128
00:07:54.299 --> 00:07:57.681
I hope that tonight we will be able to solve this mystery!"
